  "implemented_scope": [
    "Definition User/Property named-row insertion, stable native identities through rename, removal and empty local-section insertion/removal through the native owned transaction; exact existing-cell editing remains available.",
    "Scoped reference rewriting preserves string literals, canonicalizes numeric Sheet aliases and refuses referenced deletion or partial/suppressed inherited overrides; public source deltas and typed author metadata remain aligned.",
    "Successful-save source row/section addresses and bounded retained XML support undo/redo after save; opaque attributes/children and ancestor namespace declarations survive restoration. Immutable-source validation is cached by resource identity; row patching uses address/ID indexes and bounded cancellation checks.",
    "Definition projection is calculated output rather than a new literal canvas edit; inherited F/U and imported geometry caches survive native commit/undo/save. Deletion references are checked after pending native page changes reach the completed public package.",
    "Connector paste remaps connector and node references, field/run metadata and source IDs together; complete connector layer membership participates in model/runtime/drawing/public writers, layer editing and background foreground-context fields.",
    "Native pointer move/resize and finish-interaction commits reject protected roots/descendants and locked group connectors atomically, preserving formulas, undo, dirty state and committed geometry.",
    "Definition worker failures stay visible in their owned native panel/status instead of opening a duplicate blocking error alert."
  ],
